<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reginald II, Duke of Guelders</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1295–1343</span> · Also known as Reinald II of Guelders, Reginald the Black</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reginald II, called the Black, was Count of Guelders from 1326 and its first duke from 1339, when Emperor Louis IV raised it to a duchy. He enlarged the territory and strengthened its finances through tolls on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. Married to Eleanor, sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a>, he was an ally of Edward at the start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reginald-ii-duke-of-guelders.jpg" alt="Reginald II, Duke of Guelders" width="276" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The medieval artist from Glasgow · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reginald_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
